  pageNumberText: {fileID: 1362616195}
  previousButton: {fileID: 1117941945}
  nextButton: {fileID: 752606383}
  closeBookButton: {fileID: 1987051086}
  diaryPages:
  - 'March 3


    Mom said things would become better after the wedding. I want
    to believe her, but the house feels quieter whenever he comes home.'
  - 'April 16


    He was drinking again. I heard them arguing in the kitchen. Mom
    told me to lock my door and pretend I was asleep.'
  - 'May 9


    He tried my door last night. I pushed the chair against it. In the
    morning he laughed and said I was imagining things.'
  - 'May 21


    I told Mom I was afraid. She cried and said we had nowhere else
    to go. I know she is afraid too.'
  - 'June 2


    I hid the fruit knife beside my bed. I do not want to hurt anyone.
    I only want him to stay away.'
  - 'June 7


    Mom is working tonight. I locked the door twice. If he comes in
    again, I have to protect myself.'
  playerMovement: {fileID: 0}
  playerLook: {fileID: 0}
  playerInteraction: {fileID: 0}
